Two 4.0 changes hit you, plus one dependency.

1. The class org.apache.kafka.common.security.oauthbearer.secured.OAuthBearerLoginCallbackHandler was removed; use org.apache.kafka.common.security.oauthbearer.OAuthBearerLoginCallbackHandler.
2. Since 4.0 the token endpoint must be allowed with a JVM system property whose default is an empty list. Start the service with
-Dorg.apache.kafka.sasl.oauthbearer.allowed.urls=https://idp.example.internal/realms/kafka/protocol/openid-connect/token
3. The default OAUTHBEARER implementation needs jackson-databind, an optional dependency: add it to the build.

