The default JWT retriever uses the client credentials grant for an https token URL, so nothing else is needed. Without the system property the client refuses the URL with 'cannot be accessed due to restrictions'.

Bug first: NewPartitions takes the new total count, not the increment. NewPartitions(topic, 12) on a 24-partition topic asks to shrink it; on your fresh dev topic it happened to work.

Checks the docs call for: never on internal topics; keyed topics change key placement (hash(key) % partitions), break per-key order and get no redistribution, so require sign-off; no reduction; tell the team that consumers on auto.offset.reset=latest can miss records on new partitions.

INTERNAL = {"__consumer_offsets", "__transaction_state", "__share_group_state", "__cluster_metadata"}

def apply_request(req, approved_keyed=False):
    topic, add = req["topic"], int(req["add"])
    if topic in INTERNAL or topic.startswith("__"):
        raise ValueError("internal topic: refused")
    if add <= 0:
        raise ValueError("partitions can only be increased")
    if req.get("keyed") and not approved_keyed:
        raise PermissionError("keyed topic: key-to-partition mapping and ordering change; needs sign-off")
    md = admin.list_topics(topic, timeout=10)
    tm = md.topics[topic]
    if tm.error is not None:
        raise RuntimeError(str(tm.error))
    new_total = len(tm.partitions) + add
    np = [NewPartitions(topic, new_total)]
    for f in admin.create_partitions(np, validate_only=True).values():
        f.result()
    for f in admin.create_partitions(np, request_timeout=30).values():
        f.result()
    notify(req["team"], "consumers with auto.offset.reset=latest may miss records on new partitions")
    return new_total

Missing rows: put() may buffer, but then flush() must write. Connect calls flush(currentOffsets) when it commits offsets and assumes everything up to them is stored. Your task has no flush() and fires inserts without waiting, so after a restart or rebalance the buffered or failed rows are lost.
Empty DLQ: errors.tolerance and the DLQ cover converter and transformation errors; a record your code catches must be reported through the ErrantRecordReporter.
```java
private final List<Row> buffer = new ArrayList<>();
private final List<CompletableFuture<Void>> pending = new ArrayList<>();
private ErrantRecordReporter reporter;

@Override public void start(Map<String, String> props) {
    client = WarehouseClient.connect(props.get("warehouse.url"), props.get("warehouse.token"));
    reporter = context.errantRecordReporter(); // null if no DLQ
}

@Override public void put(Collection<SinkRecord> records) {
    for (SinkRecord r : records) {
        try {
            buffer.add(Row.from(r.value()));
        } catch (Exception e) {
            if (reporter != null) reporter.report(r, e);
            else throw new ConnectException("Bad record " + r.topic() + "-" + r.kafkaPartition() + "@" + r.kafkaOffset(), e);
        }
    }
    if (buffer.size() >= 5000) sendBuffer();
}

private void sendBuffer() {
    if (buffer.isEmpty()) return;
    pending.add(client.bulkInsertAsync(new ArrayList<>(buffer)));
    buffer.clear();
}

@Override public void flush(Map<TopicPartition, OffsetAndMetadata> currentOffsets) {
    sendBuffer();
    try {
        CompletableFuture.allOf(pending.toArray(new CompletableFuture[0])).join();
    } catch (CompletionException e) {
        throw new ConnectException("Warehouse write failed", e.getCause());
    } finally {
        pending.clear();
    }
}
```

The draft misses replicas in three ways: it looks only at leaders, it never sees internal topics, and the user can only see topics starting with app-. Grant ci-gate in its KafkaUser: topic, name *, patternType literal, operation Describe; cluster, operation Describe.
```java
public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
    Set<Integer> ids = Arrays.stream(args).map(Integer::valueOf).collect(Collectors.toSet());
    int found = 0;
    try (Admin admin = Admin.create(loadProps("/etc/ci-gate/client.properties"))) {
        Set<String> topics = admin.listTopics(new ListTopicsOptions().listInternal(true))
                                  .names().get(60, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
        Map<String, TopicDescription> desc = admin.describeTopics(topics)
                                  .allTopicNames().get(60, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
        for (TopicDescription td : desc.values())
            for (TopicPartitionInfo p : td.partitions())
                for (Node n : p.replicas())
                    if (ids.contains(n.id())) {
                        System.err.printf("replica on %d: %s-%d%n", n.id(), td.name(), p.partition());
                        found++;
                    }
        Map<TopicPartition, PartitionReassignment> moving =
            admin.listPartitionReassignments().reassignments().get(60, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
        if (!moving.isEmpty()) {
            System.err.println("reassignment in progress for " + moving.size() + " partitions");
            found++;
        }
    } catch (Exception e) {
        System.err.println("gate error: " + e);
        System.exit(2);
    }
    if (found > 0) System.exit(1);
    System.out.println("OK");
}
