public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
  KafkaStreams streams = new KafkaStreams(RoutePlanner.build(), loadProps());
  // the 4.x handler (one argument); set before start()
  streams.setUncaughtExceptionHandler(e -> {
    Throwable c = e;
    while (c != null) {
      if (c instanceof RetriableException) return StreamThreadExceptionResponse.REPLACE_THREAD;
      c = c.getCause();
    }
    return StreamThreadExceptionResponse.SHUTDOWN_CLIENT;
  });
  HttpServer http = HttpServer.create(new InetSocketAddress(8080), 0);
  http.createContext("/healthz", ex -> {
    KafkaStreams.State s = streams.state();
    int code = (s == KafkaStreams.State.ERROR || s == KafkaStreams.State.PENDING_ERROR) ? 503 : 200;
    ex.sendResponseHeaders(code, -1);
    ex.close();
  });
  Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook(new Thread(() -> {
    streams.close(CloseOptions.groupMembershipOperation(CloseOptions.GroupMembershipOperation.LEAVE_GROUP)
        .withTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(45)));
    http.stop(0);
  }));
  http.start();
  streams.start();
}

Notes: the Thread.UncaughtExceptionHandler overload the guide still shows was removed in 4.0, and the handler can only be set before start(). PENDING_ERROR and ERROR are terminal, so the probe must fail on both. By default close() does not leave the group; LEAVE_GROUP (org.apache.kafka.streams.CloseOptions, 4.2+) triggers the rebalance at once. Keep the 45 s timeout under the 60 s grace period, after which the kubelet kills the process.

The join is fine. customers is a versioned table, so a stream-table join looks up the customer version whose timestamp is the latest one at or before the order's timestamp. Your only customer record has timestamp t0+5 s and the order t0, so there is no version yet, and the inner join drops the order. An unversioned store would pass because it joins the latest record by offset, which is the behaviour you chose to avoid. Only stream-side records trigger the join, so pipe table records first.

class OrderEnricherTest {
  TopologyTestDriver driver; TestInputTopic<String, Customer> customersIn;
  TestInputTopic<String, Order> ordersIn; TestOutputTopic<String, Order> out;
  final Instant t0 = Instant.parse("2026-11-20T10:00:00Z");
  @BeforeEach void setUp() { /* driver, createInputTopic x2, createOutputTopic as before */ }
  @AfterEach void tearDown() { driver.close(); }

  @Test void enrichesOrder() {
    customersIn.pipeInput("c-17", new Customer("c-17", "Old Street 1"), t0);
    ordersIn.pipeInput("c-17", new Order("o-1", 4200), t0.plusSeconds(5));
    assertEquals("Old Street 1", out.readKeyValue().value.address());
    assertTrue(out.isEmpty());
  }

  @Test void keepsAddressValidAtOrderTime() {
    customersIn.pipeInput("c-17", new Customer("c-17", "Old Street 1"), t0);
    customersIn.pipeInput("c-17", new Customer("c-17", "New Road 9"), t0.plusSeconds(10));
    ordersIn.pipeInput("c-17", new Order("o-2", 990), t0.plusSeconds(5));
    assertEquals("Old Street 1", out.readKeyValue().value.address());
    assertTrue(out.isEmpty());
  }
}
